<section xml:id="section-lintrans-matrix-terminology">

<title>Terminology and notation</title>

<p>

The first two definitions below apply to a linear transformation <m>\funcdef{T}{V}{W}</m> between finite-dimensional vector spaces <m>V</m> and <m>W</m>,
along with some choice of bases <m>\basisfont{B}</m> and <m>\basisfont{B}'</m> of <m>V</m> and <m>W</m>,
respectively.

<dl width="medium">

	<li>
	<title> <term>matrix of <m>T</m></term> relative to <m>\basisfont{B}, \basisfont{B}'</m> </title>
	<!-- TODO index -->
	<p>
	the standard matrix of the composition
	<m>\invcoordmap{B} T \coordmap{B'}</m>,
	which is a transformation <m>\R^n \to \R^m</m> in the real case or
	a transformation <m>\C^n \to \C^m</m> in the complex case,
	and where <m>n = \dim V</m> and <m>m = \dim W</m>
	</p>
	</li>

</dl>

<dl width="narrow"><li>
	<title><m>\matrixOf{T}{B'B}</m></title>
	<p> notation for the <term>matrix of <m>T</m> relative to <m>\basisfont{B}</m> and <m>\basisfont{B}'</m></term> </p>
</li></dl>

The next two definitions apply to a linear operator <m>\funcdef{T}{V}{V}</m>.
In the first,
<m>V</m> is assumed to be finite-dimensional,
and <m>\basisfont{B}</m> is some basis of <m>V</m> that is chosen to represent both a basis for the domain space of <m>T</m> and the codomain space of <m>T</m>
(which are the same space in this case).

<dl width="narrow">

	<li>
	<title><m>\matrixOf{T}{B}</m></title>
	<p> notation for the <term>matrix of <m>T</m> relative to <m>\basisfont{B}</m></term> </p>
	</li>

	<li>
	<title><m>T^\ell</m></title>
	<p> notation for composition of <m>\abs{\ell}</m> copies of either <m>T</m> (<m>\ell</m> positive) or <m>\inv{T}</m> (<m>\ell</m> negative) </p>
	</li>

</dl>

</p>

</section>
